## 2. Gameplay design

We should make the opening playable, but not turn it into an obstacle course. The player should feel present in the scene.

### Player controls

| Input          | Action                                    |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| WASD           | Move Harsha                               |
| Mouse          | Rotate camera                             |
| Shift          | Walk faster                               |
| E              | Contextual interaction                    |
| Mouse movement | Look around during cinematic-free moments |

Movement design:

- Default movement should be walking, not running.
- No jumping or combat.
- No health bar, inventory, quest list, or unnecessary HUD.
- No objective markers floating above objects.
- Movement should feel relaxed and grounded.

### Player interactions

| Interaction            | Behaviour                                         |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Look at surroundings   | Camera follows the player's view                  |
| Phone vibrates         | Cinematic takes over briefly                      |
| Read message           | Phone screen is shown clearly                     |
| Resume walking         | Player regains control                            |
| Look toward headlights | Camera gently assists without forcing a full lock |
| Car stops              | Player control ends for the chapter transition    |

I recommend only one essential interaction: reading the message. Everything else should emerge naturally from movement and observation.

