The opening should feel familiar, not like a horror game.

### Visual elements

- Residential buildings with a few illuminated windows.
- Warm streetlights with pools of light on the road.
- Parked vehicles.
- Occasional trees and roadside details.
- Subtle reflections on the road.
- Distant traffic lights and moving headlights.
- Darker areas at the edges of the street.

### Lighting progression

| Stage           | Lighting                                      |
| --------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Opening         | Neutral warm street lighting                  |
| Phone message   | Phone glow illuminates hands and face         |
| Walking resumes | Normal street lighting                        |
| Car approaches  | Headlights introduce strong directional light |
| Chapter ending  | Red tail lights against a dark street         |

Keep the scene readable. Darkness should create uncertainty, not make the player unable to see.

## 6. Audio and cinematic effects

Audio will do a lot of the storytelling here.

| Moment          | Audio                                               |
| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Opening         | Quiet nighttime ambience                            |
| Walking         | Footsteps synchronized to movement                  |
| Phone message   | Short vibration                                     |
| Reading         | Very subtle phone interaction sound                 |
| Walking resumes | Footsteps return                                    |
| Car appears     | Distant engine                                      |
| Car approaches  | Engine gradually grows louder                       |
| Car stops       | Engine slows, brake and tire sounds                 |
| Chapter end     | Ambient sound fades into a short low cinematic tone |

No horror stingers. No screaming, aggressive impacts, or jump scares. We want curiosity and suspense.

